    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. so if we're looking at zip codes, how do we distinguish between a neighborhood that's \"volatile\" due to transient populations vs one that's just in a transition phase? like, if a neighborhood has a lot of high-turnover renters or a high concentration of certain types of local businesses (like bodegas or discount stores vs organic markets), does that statistically correlate to a higher default risk in your experience?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
